{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Awake.</b> Milraʿ, and so many [others]." "<b>Clothe yourself with strength.</b> For clothing is an ornament to the arm." "<b>Who struck Rahab.</b> The champions of victory, and like it: \"He did not turn to Rahabim\" (Psalms 40:5). I will mention Rahab and Babylon [Psalms 87:4]." "<b>Who pierced.</b> From the root חול, as in אחז (Exodus 15:14). And the meaning concerns the signs that were done in Egypt." "<b>And the tanin.</b> That is Pharaoh, and so it is written in the book of Ezekiel: \"the great tanin\" (Ezekiel 29:3)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:00.622784165Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}